    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "When the Pacific Electric Railway arrived in 1906, the station adopted the name 'Cypress,' replacing the earlier 'Waterville' to avoid duplication in the system.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cypressca.org/resident/cypress-70"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city’s annual Cypress Community Festival, held every July at Oak Knoll Park, is one of Orange County’s largest single‑day celebrations.",
